16. CLOUDFRONT REQUEST FLOW
====================================================================

User requests:

    https://example.com/index.html


STEP 1

DNS directs the request to CloudFront.


STEP 2

CloudFront receives the viewer request.


STEP 3

CloudFront determines the appropriate edge location.


STEP 4

CloudFront checks its cache.


If content exists:

    CACHE HIT


If content does not exist:

    CACHE MISS


STEP 5

For a cache miss, CloudFront requests the content
from the origin.


STEP 6

Origin returns the response.


STEP 7

CloudFront returns the response to the user.


STEP 8

CloudFront may cache the response according to the
cache behavior/policy.


AWS describes this cache-miss flow: CloudFront requests the
object from the origin, receives it at the edge, forwards it
to the viewer, and adds it to cache for subsequent requests. :contentReference[oaicite:8]{index=8}


