55. ONE-MINUTE INTERVIEW ANSWER
===============================

"Cloud service models describe how infrastructure and software
responsibilities are divided between the customer and the provider.

In an on-premises environment, the organization owns and manages the
physical infrastructure, operating systems and applications.

With IaaS, the cloud provider manages the underlying physical
infrastructure while the customer manages the operating system and
application. AWS EC2 is a common example.

With PaaS, the provider also manages much of the operating system and
application platform, allowing developers to focus mainly on their
application. AWS Elastic Beanstalk is an example.

With SaaS, the provider manages the complete application and
underlying infrastructure, while the customer simply uses and
configures the software. Gmail, Salesforce and Microsoft 365 are
examples."

